  "news_profile": "These records are retrieval queries/captions. Preserve all modifiers and referential details exactly; do not simplify them. These are news photo captions and headlines, often with missing punctuation. Preserve personal names and names of groups, performers, organisations and brands. For example, the name 'Idiots of Ants' stays 'Idiots of Ants', not a literal Polish phrase. A positional 'left' or 'right' after a person's name describes their position in a photo: 'Henry Kissinger left chats with Elie Wiesel' means 'Henry Kissinger (po lewej) rozmawia z Elie Wieselem', not that he left a conversation. Use this reading when supported by syntax; do not invent positions. Weathered means showing wear from weather ('noszący ślady działania warunków atmosferycznych'), never 'pogodzony'. Preserve corrupted/merged numbers rather than guessing a percentage or date range. You may restore missing punctuation when the syntax is clear. Check Polish grammar and agreement in full sentences, including constructions such as 'kilka osób stoi'."
